figdown 0.3 flowchart
# `DRAWN-ANNOTATION-FORM`: `note=` on the four acceptors the `flowchart` genre owns
# — `process`, `decision`, `terminator` and `flowline`.
#
# `CATEGORICAL-MEANING-MAPPING`'s standing rule is why they are listed at all: EACH GENRE DECLARES ITS
# OWN VOCABULARY SEPARATELY, even when the list is identical to another
# genre's. `process`/`decision`/`terminator` are `node` under a role (`FLOWCHART-ROLE-KEYWORDS`)
# and `flowline` is `edge` renamed (`GENRE-CONNECTOR-SPELLING`), so it would have been possible to
# let them inherit the key silently from the shapes they are built on. They
# do not: each row in DIRECTIVE_OPTS names `note` itself, and this fixture is
# what would go red if one of them were dropped on the assumption that the
# block genre's row covers it.
#
# `decision` is the carrier worth having a fixture for on its own: a diamond
# has no flat side to sit a box against, so it is the shape most likely to
# push its note out to a leader line. That is a RENDERER fact and is not in
# the model (core §12.7).
#
# See case 800 for the GOLDEN GAP that applies here too: normalize.js does not
# project `note`, so this fixture pins acceptance, not the strings.
#
# EXPERIMENTAL-ADJACENT, NORMATIVE BY SUBJECT. `flowchart` is an experimental
# GENRE (`CONSTRUCT-STATUS-TIERS`), which by STATUS.txt's first criterion would put a fixture with
# this header in conformance/experimental/. Read that before quoting this
# file's bucket: its subject is the NORMATIVE key `note=`, but its header is
# not, and the maintainer criterion is decided by the header for genre cases.
process ingest "Ingest frame" note="on a process"
decision drop "Over the threshold?" note="on a decision — a diamond has no flat side, so this is the hardest note to place"
terminator done "Forwarded" note="on a terminator"
terminator dropped "Dropped"
flowline ingest -> drop note="on a flowline — flowchart's connector, and `edge` under another name"
flowline drop -[yes]-> dropped note="a labelled flowline takes both keys at once"
flowline drop -[no]-> done
